    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p9-q18-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Explain why every prime number greater than 3 has a remainder of 1 or 5 when divided by 6.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Remainders 0, 2 and 4 give even numbers, and remainder 3 gives a multiple of 3. A prime greater than 3 must therefore have remainder 1 or 5.",
          "worked": "Every integer has one of the forms $6n$, $6n+1$, $6n+2$, $6n+3$, $6n+4$ or $6n+5$. A number greater than 3 of the form $6n$, $6n+2$ or $6n+4$ is even and cannot be prime. A number greater than 3 of the form $6n+3$ is divisible by 3 and cannot be prime. Only $6n+1$ and $6n+5$ remain, giving remainders 1 and 5.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q18-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Suppose $p>5$ is a prime number. Using (a), prove that $p^2-1$ is always divisible by 24.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For $p=6n+1$, $p^2-1=12n(3n+1)$. For $p=6n+5$, $p^2-1=12n(3n+5)+24$.\n\nIn each case the product following 12 is even, so $p^2-1$ is divisible by 24.",
          "worked": "By (a), $p=6n+1$ or $p=6n+5$ for an integer $n$.\n\nIf $p=6n+1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}p^2-1&=(6n+1)^2-1\\\\p^2-1&=36n^2+12n+1-1\\\\p^2-1&=12n(3n+1).\\end{align*}$$\nIf $n$ is even, $n(3n+1)$ is even. If $n$ is odd, $3n+1$ is even. Thus $p^2-1$ is divisible by 24.\n\nIf $p=6n+5$:\n$$\\begin{align*}p^2-1&=(6n+5)^2-1\\\\p^2-1&=36n^2+60n+24\\\\p^2-1&=12n(3n+5)+24.\\end{align*}$$\nIf $n$ is even, $n(3n+5)$ is even. If $n$ is odd, $3n+5$ is even. Both terms are therefore divisible by 24. Hence $p^2-1$ is divisible by 24 in both cases.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 108
      }
    ]
  },
